module gunbc.plans.factory_dogfood

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.markdown_helpers { h2, p, li, ul, ol, quote }

fn factory_dogfood_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**This plan is written as an intention** (`gunbc.design_argument::plans_are_intentions`): what the repository should become, why, and done-when. How it is realized is downstream; the work items live under `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority` (the `fabric-bringup`, `vm-service` and `factory` projects) and name this intention."),
      p(text: "**Grounding:** `gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed` (a published property with no receipt is not published), `gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder` (a service dimension stays opaque only above a falsifiable quality floor with a named consequence), `gunbc.design_argument::consumption` (a dependency is admitted by its consumer), `gunbc.design_argument::selection_precedes_convergence`, `gunbc.design_argument::epistemic_humility`."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "1. Intention"),
    p(text: "**What:** a selected work item travels through fabric dispatch, durable execution, implementation, exact-head verification, publication, independent review, manager acceptance and merge; interruption and restart lose no state; the operator does not hand-integrate it. Split from the first-customer service on 2026-11-17 (the program review: two goals with different consumers, risks and evidence; `gunbc.plans.first_customer_service` holds the other)."),
    p(text: "**Why:** the factory exists to turn every other project's tasks into landed, verified changes without the operator's time (`factory`'s own contribution to the root). Today the operator hand-integrates, hand-redeploys the lab, runs the merge-head check per pull request and accepts every node, so their time is the throughput limit of every program, this one included. The cost removed is operator time per landing."),
    p(text: "**Done when** (each assessed against the tree or against a receipt unless marked as the operator's judgement):"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "One request has travelled the whole factory on the real route and come back as an independently reviewed, published candidate, read by the acceptance function of `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dogfood_route` from the durable records of one attempt (`factory-dogfood-route`'s handback: the dogfood start receipt)."),
      li(text: "Every step a change traverses (orientation, implementation, test, commit, publication, review, verification) survives process death and controller restart as workflow-owned durable state (`factory`'s red control)."),
      li(text: "The required CI verdict names what it executed and is published from an admitted receipt for the exact commit (`ci-end-to-end-execution`, `work-exec-5-ci-verdict-from-receipt`)."),
      li(text: "The dogfood route is accepted only with exact-head verification evidence: the verifier establishes what ran for exactly which commit (`ci-executed-coverage-receipt`, now a declared parent of `factory-dogfood-route`), because an independently reviewed candidate over an unverified head is not the factory (the program review's correction)."),
      li(text: "Operator's judgement: the dogfood window has run long enough on the real route for the operator to trust the factory with the first-customer service's work (`gunbc.plans.first_customer_service`)."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "2. The backward structure, read at e346a2c89daa"),
    p(text: "This program has no declared dependency edges. `vm-service`, `factory-dogfood-route`, `factory` and `fabric-bringup` are related only by project membership, and `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority` declares no edge among the roughly sixty nodes under `fabric-bringup`, `vm-service`, `factory`, `factory-on-fabric`, `work-execution-redesign`, `ci-end-to-end-execution` and their siblings. The order lives in prose: `factory-dogfood-route` names the stages its receipt still owes to other changes, and `fabric-bringup` says in its red control that work gated on the fabric does not dispatch until it is accepted. So the backward walk below is read from node text, and its first realization obligation is to declare these edges so that a manager can read the path instead of re-deriving it."),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**The goal.** The dogfood window runs on the real route and its receipts are what the first-customer service rests on (`service-evidence-capture` pins the window's joined evidence to the start receipt)."),
      li(text: "**Just before it.** The dogfood start receipt exists: one complete attempt on the real route, every stage established by its own typed record (`factory-dogfood-route`)."),
      li(text: "**The stages the receipt still owes**, each to the change that writes its own record: G1 cutover (immutable subject, shared computation), G5 isolated execution (a record binding the granted unit's observed start and exit to its grant and fence), G3 metering (a Final metering record), G4 request binding and result returned. The attempt and lease duplicate beside fabric is deleted first (`factory-attempt-execution-on-fabric-lease`), because the srv1 lab defects of 2026-11-04 are its symptoms and every belt fix is work the cutover deletes."),
      li(text: "**Before any of that is observable.** The lab serves the head it was built from (`lab-standings-track-main` and `lab-converges-release-pair`, gunb-ai/gunbc#16592): until the lab tracks main, a new plan node appears only after a hand redeploy, the workspace page cannot decode the `retired` event kind, and no acceptance can be read from the workspace at all."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Today's frontier**, read the same way: the lab pair; the belt-beside-fabric audit and cut; the owed dogfood stages (G1, G3, G4, G5) in whichever order their owners pick; and the required-verdict-from-receipt chain (`work-exec-5-ci-verdict-from-receipt`). The SCM rows under `factory` are gated on the fabric by `fabric-bringup`'s own rule and are not on this path."),
    h2(text: "3. Layers of work, prioritized against the goals, and where it stalled before (2026-11-17)"),
    p(text: "The operator's staging rule (`gunbc.plans.planning_consolidation` section 7): work is layered, each layer justified by the goal it unblocks and sized by what the tree shows. This program stalled several times, and each stall is on record, so each layer names the stall it is shaped to avoid."),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**Layer 0, the lab serves the head it was built from.** `lab-standings-track-main`, `lab-converges-release-pair` (gunb-ai/gunbc#16592). Goal: anything else in this program becomes observable. Stall avoided: the operator hand-redeploying srv1 (about 19 minutes a time) to see a plan change, and a served binary that cannot decode the event log it is shown."),
      li(text: "**Layer 1, one execution model.** `factory-attempt-execution-on-fabric-lease`: the belt's own attempt, lease, slot and capture state deleted into fabric's (`gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle`, `product.capacity.lease`), after the audit that names what execution needs from each belt module. Goal: the dogfood route's records come from one writer. Stall avoided: the three srv1 lab defects of 2026-11-04 were symptoms of the duplicate; every fix made on the belt is work the cutover deletes."),
      li(text: "**Layer 2, the owed dogfood stages, each as its own record.** G3 metering (gunb-ai/gunbc#13073) and G4 request binding and result returned (gunb-ai/gunbc#13075) landed in October. G1 shared computation (`dogfood-g1-shared-computation-record`) did not: gunb-ai/gunbc#13097 was a stacked PR whose base kept moving, conflicted with main in the generated emit file, carried seven witness failures identical on main, and closed unmerged on 2026-10-09. G5 isolated execution (`dogfood-g5-isolated-execution-record`) has no record yet. Goal: `factory-dogfood-route`'s receipt reads every stage. Stall avoided: stacked work against a moving base; each record lands alone against main, after layer 1, so there is one writer to bind to."),
      li(text: "**Layer 3, the start receipt and the dogfood window.** `factory-dogfood-route` read complete by its acceptance function; `service-evidence-capture` pinning the window's joined evidence; the live views that watch it (`fabric-worker-event-log`, then `serve-held-open-response`, both authored 2026-10-05 with no attempts since) following the 2026-10-05 ruling that streaming goes through the fabric. Goal: the operator's yes to an external customer rests on receipts. Stall avoided: evidence added late loses the window it should have covered."),
      li(text: "**Layer 4, the required verdict from an admitted receipt.** The work-execution chain `work-exec-0` to `work-exec-6` (already edged), ending with the required CI verdict published from a receipt for the exact commit and one ledger per host. Goal: the factory's verification half names what it executed (`ci-executed-coverage-receipt`, `ci-end-to-end-execution`). Stall avoided: a check that reported failures for days while executing nothing."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**The stall that is not a layer.** 52 roadmap texts wait on \"the reviewed contracts document\": the six F nodes under `factory-on-fabric` and `microvm-runtime-durable-state` (F1 pool on the live line, F2 every attempt takes a seat, F3 host budget, F4 builds keyed on Rust inputs, F5 off the control host, F6 scoped worker grants) have been DRAFT since 2026-10-01 pending a document that has no path in the tree and was never produced. This intention is that document's replacement: each F node is re-cut against the layer it belongs to (F1 and F2 to layer 1, F5 to layer 2's G5 record, F6 to the G0 question) or retired, by the operator's word. Until then they are not reported as blocked on anything real."),
    h2(text: "4. What is outside this intention"),
    p(text: "Everything the service promises to a customer (admission, isolation, metering, billing, recovery, health) is `gunbc.plans.first_customer_service`; the harness alignment rows and the SCM rows are not prerequisites of the dogfood start receipt and are ranked against it by the operator."),
    h2(text: "5. Open questions"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**G0, `contained-development-execution`.** A draft portfolio gate (no boundary, no red control, no edges, no contracts document after six weeks) that forbids new autonomous dispatch while the current process already dispatches autonomous workers. The 2026-10-03 ruling set the dogfood bar at a capped systemd unit plus a lease. Either G0 gets a first slice (`factory-f6-scoped-worker-grants`) and a boundary, or it is retired to a ruling; it must not stay an undefined standing veto on the route this plan converges on."),
      li(text: "**The realization home** for execution and work items (`gunbc.plans.planning_consolidation` section 6): the dogfood route's records are written by the belt today and by fabric after the cut, and the receipt must read the same records before and after."),
      li(text: "**Which stage is first.** The owners of G1, G3, G4 and G5 are named in `factory-dogfood-route`'s first slice by pull request number, not by node; the realization that picks this up names the node for each and declares the edges."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "6. Realization"),
    p(text: "The layers of section 3 are realized by the existing nodes they name plus two minted 2026-11-17 for the stages that had none, `dogfood-g1-shared-computation-record` and `dogfood-g5-isolated-execution-record`, with edges declared from `factory-dogfood-route` to its stage records and to the execution cut, and from `fabric-worker-event-log` and `service-evidence-capture` to the route. They may be redrawn without this plan changing. What a landing reports is which owed stage's record now exists, read by the dogfood receipt's acceptance function, never a count of nodes closed."),
  ]
}

data factory_dogfood_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "factory-dogfood",
  title: "Factory dogfood: a work item lands and is verified without the operator",
  body: factory_dogfood_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Section 1 is achieved: the dogfood start receipt is read by the acceptance function, the factory's and vm-service's red controls hold on the tree, and the operator has said yes to an external customer.") },
}
